If \\alpha^{2}\\beta\\ll 1 (thus \\alpha^{-1}\\gg\\beta^{1/2}\\gg\\alpha\\beta), the evolution of the expanding shell can be divided into two regimes. The first regime is from \\tau\\sim\\tau_{0} to \\tau\\sim\\beta^{1/2}. During this period, since \\alpha\\tau\\ll 1, the radioactive source g(\\tau)=\\alpha e^{-\\alpha\\tau} can be approximated by g(\\tau)\\approx\\alpha. Inserting g(\\tau)\\approx\\alpha into Eq. (11), we get

